                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e5f2f7f5-c414-42d6-80ad-f402b3cc597f",
                        "source_entry_id": "8582e31a-fac1-3321-b61a-c29f064a4cb5",
                        "source_sense_id": "e3fe3575-cf3b-3f8c-b62b-6cc767b26bf0",
                        "target_lang_word": "Mangrove",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Mangrove",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1ba8e18f-27b2-3c81-928e-963458f7b309",
                                        "entry_id": "f7060cc3-bd89-3691-84b0-603ef6df7486",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Gehölz, das durch spezielle morphologische und physiologische Anpassungen in der Gezeitenzone tropischer und subtropischer Küsten gedeihen kann"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "42313c16-b1d8-4ef7-a6ee-9d670ac5c204",
                                                "sense_id": "1ba8e18f-27b2-3c81-928e-963458f7b309",
                                                "text": "Mangroven kommen mit den schwierigen Wuchsbedingungen an der Meeresküste bestens klar."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8b1904ba-464f-4e45-8c94-bbc939c99aea",
                                                "sense_id": "1ba8e18f-27b2-3c81-928e-963458f7b309",
                                                "text": "„Bald darauf war er zwischen den Mangroven verschwunden.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8dd59066-582e-3f6a-a95c-7dd92be0d51d",
                                        "entry_id": "f7060cc3-bd89-3691-84b0-603ef6df7486",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "von Mangroven^([1]) dominiertes Ökosystem in der Gezeitenzone tropischer und subtropischer Küsten"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Pflanzengeographie"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2b97379e-c954-4376-8ae4-d0ef03b692ec",
                                                "sense_id": "8dd59066-582e-3f6a-a95c-7dd92be0d51d",
                                                "text": "Die sehr artenreichen Mangroven sind vor allem durch Tourismus und Fischereiwirtschaft stark bedroht."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"2\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "add81c77-ce77-42eb-b891-f54636fd1e06",
                        "source_entry_id": "8582e31a-fac1-3321-b61a-c29f064a4cb5",
                        "source_sense_id": "e3fe3575-cf3b-3f8c-b62b-6cc767b26bf0",
                        "target_lang_word": "mangrove",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "mangrove",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "16a43b54-fa0a-3840-83fb-e3ea91e4801b",
                                        "entry_id": "b0d918a3-4712-384b-96ec-1cca8e73879e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any of various tropical and subtropical evergreen shrubs or trees chiefly of the Rhizophoraceae family that have aerial roots and grow in clumps in brackish intertidal coastal areas; (specifically) any of various trees of the genus Rhizophora, especially the red mangrove (Rhizophora mangle)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3e29f9ec-52ff-48ac-8f63-3edba513c653",
                                                "sense_id": "16a43b54-fa0a-3840-83fb-e3ea91e4801b",
                                                "text": "The channel by which we went to, and returned from Olinda, was bordered on each side by mangroves, which sprang like a miniature forest out of the greasy mud-banks. The bright green colour of these bushes always reminded me of the rank grass in a churchyard: both are nourished by putrid exhalations; the one speaks of death past, and the other too often of death to come."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "128a1035-fadc-40da-b579-86f3be3b4f86",
                                                "sense_id": "16a43b54-fa0a-3840-83fb-e3ea91e4801b",
                                                "text": "We called […] in and out of rivers, streams of death in life, whose banks were rotting into mud, whose waters, thickened into slime, invaded the contorted mangroves, that seemed to writhe at us in the extremity of an impotent despair."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c1bf2d45-5477-446c-8916-ac4d30df0f32",
                                                "sense_id": "16a43b54-fa0a-3840-83fb-e3ea91e4801b",
                                                "text": "The team that found the species living in a mangrove forest also included Thai wildlife YouTuber JoCho Sippawat, who is also an author on the paper published last week."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1e3923bc-64dc-4c03-afe5-3750d8671862",
                                                "sense_id": "16a43b54-fa0a-3840-83fb-e3ea91e4801b",
                                                "text": "This lush forest, just a few miles from the Guatemalan border, teems with diverse wildlife – from crocodiles and crabs to fish darting through seemingly endless mangroves. […] The Barra de Santiago is bordered on one side by mangroves with the ocean on the other; the project will be the first to build houses on the mangrove side."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ac265ae8-968f-3e3d-977f-0fec0ce83084",
                                        "entry_id": "b0d918a3-4712-384b-96ec-1cca8e73879e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A forest of such shrubs or trees."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "547e8ecd-ed3d-3d07-bac5-04fcaea4d8cf",
                                        "entry_id": "b0d918a3-4712-384b-96ec-1cca8e73879e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Preceded by a descriptive word: any of various shrubs or trees of genera other than Rhizophora which resemble plants of this genus in appearance and habitat."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "49e0aaa4-56c9-37d2-8d72-d817f707395b",
                                        "entry_id": "b0d918a3-4712-384b-96ec-1cca8e73879e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Synonym of mangal (“a tropical and subtropical coastal intertidal swampland ecosystem characterized by mangroves (sense 1) or similar shrubs and trees”)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "also",
                                            "attributive",
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "76f703f6-0184-47db-91af-dc6a3bdf1656",
                                                "sense_id": "49e0aaa4-56c9-37d2-8d72-d817f707395b",
                                                "text": "There has been some investigation into the potential of seaweeds as a carbon store, and although more is needed, one study says that seaweed habitats are believed to be the most productive of all coastal vegetated ecosystems, and suggested that the world's seaweed sequesters as much carbon as all the planet’s seagrass meadows, saltmarshes and mangroves combined."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "59039c9e-0bbc-4f5f-87ab-d17ded70c463",
                        "source_entry_id": "8582e31a-fac1-3321-b61a-c29f064a4cb5",
                        "source_sense_id": "e3fe3575-cf3b-3f8c-b62b-6cc767b26bf0",
                        "target_lang_word": "mangrove",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "mangrove",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dd8784dd-e199-3cf6-904e-6b5da270c1c8",
                                        "entry_id": "4051c3bb-eb46-3ee5-919b-e0982a8cebe0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Formation végétale caractéristique des régions littorales de la zone tropicale, constituée de palétuviers et, selon les zones géographiques, d’espèces végétales variées."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "38eea39f-cb9e-4ecd-8a7e-2bb7f2c8c4c6",
                                                "sense_id": "dd8784dd-e199-3cf6-904e-6b5da270c1c8",
                                                "text": "En trente ans, les mangroves ont perdu 20 % de leur superficie. La prise de conscience de leur valeur est récente. Ces forêts humides offrent une multitude de services irremplaçables. Elles limitent l’érosion due aux vents, aux vagues et au courants. Elles protègent les côtes contre les intrusions d’eau salée …"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "04c3f9d8-27d5-48a6-83b8-882e64e14aa7",
                                                "sense_id": "dd8784dd-e199-3cf6-904e-6b5da270c1c8",
                                                "text": "Un ciel grisailleux couvrait la mangrove à la grande joie des moustiques porteurs de fièvre qu’il avait fallu faire fuir vitement-pressé en allumant ici et là ces grands feux de bois que les anciens appelaient charibaudées."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "249ee066-dee4-45f0-9655-47657222e0cb",
                                                "sense_id": "dd8784dd-e199-3cf6-904e-6b5da270c1c8",
                                                "text": "Cette métropole, les plaines gangétiques, la forêt et les montagnes du nord du Bengale, les régions couvertes de neige, les barrages et la rocaille du Bengale central, la mangrove des Sundarbans, les champs de maïs, les mines de charbon, les plantations de thé, où Brati s’enfuira-t-il ?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a725dca1-9a50-4db8-88e0-5079aba61d23",
                                                "sense_id": "dd8784dd-e199-3cf6-904e-6b5da270c1c8",
                                                "text": "Sur les côtes existe une formation très particulière : la Mangrove des côtes à fond vaseux. Elle pénètre dans les continents parfois jusqu’à 100 kilomètres, le long des fleuves. Les Palétuviers aux grandes béquilles en sont les éléments principaux."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
